// S-264 (W5-16 U2), §4.4 (the case of W4-16 U2/b: `let t1 = (t0, k)` and on): a chain of `let t(i) = (t(i-1), k)` has
// a size that grows by the size of `k` and one tuple shape at each statement, and the depth grows by one. Here `p` is
// `(I32, (I32, I32))` (5), `k` is `(p, p, p)` (1 + 15 = 16) and `t0` is `k`, so `t(i)` is `16 + 17 i`: `t240` is 4096
// exactly and `t241` is 4113, the first to pass the limit (its depth is 244, within the limit, so it is the size).
// E0422 at the tuple of `t241`, and `t242` and the lines after use the type that is over the limit and have no
// diagnostic.

